    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.clue\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! Is there any way to make mini.clue show up for every key press and show the keys similar to how nvzone/showkeys does it. Or is it possible to achieve this with the combination of mini.notify and mini.keymap.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi echasnovski! Is there any way to make mini.clue show up for every key press and show the keys similar to how nvzone/showkeys does it. Or is it possible to achieve this with the combination of mini.notify and mini.keymap.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nHi echasnovski! Is there any way to make mini.clue show up for every key press and show the keys similar to how nvzone/showkeys does it. Or is it possible to achieve this with the combination of mini.notify and mini.keymap.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
